  "_comment": "Shared recorded-walk parity table (#4874). Each case is one run's audit rows, every row with an explicit chain sequence, including its seed rows (pull_request_opened / fixup_pushed head_sha, integration_commit_recorded merge_sha). want_head is the unbounded acceptance head: the server resolver (backend/internal/server acceptanceHeadAsOf over walkRecordedBaseMerges) and the MCP preview mirror (backend/internal/mcpserver latestReportedHeadSHA over walkPreviewBaseMerges) must both answer it. A non-empty skip names the issue owing the fix; every case currently carries an empty skip. Both consumers assert at least 15 cases. Shas: S 5000..05 PR-open head, V 7000..07 and W 8000..08 vouched tips, M a000..01 and M2 a000..02 merge commits, F f000..01 fix-up head, I 1f00..01 integration merge, P 9000..09 a non-walked prior, X eeee..00 a foreign push.",
